Assignment 1.4 — Git Essentials I
Objective

To convert a local project into a Git repository using Git commands.

1. Check Git Installation
bash
git --version

2. Initialize Repository
bash
mkdir Assignment-1.4
cd Assignment-1.4
git init

3. Configure Git
bash
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your@email.com"

4. Create HTML File

Create index.html:

HTML
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>My First Git Project</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome to My First Git Project</h1>
    <p>Learning Git and GitHub.</p>
    <footer>Assignment 1.4</footer>
</body>
</html>

5. Check Git Status
bash
git status

6. Make Three Commits

Commit 1:

bash
git add index.html
git commit -m "Initial HTML structure"


Commit 2: Add a welcome paragraph and commit the changes.

bash
git add index.html
git commit -m "Add welcome message"


Commit 3: Add a footer and commit the changes.

bash
git add index.html
git commit -m "Add footer section"

7. Check Commit History
bash
git log --oneline

8. Conclusion

Successfully initialized a Git repository, configured Git, created an HTML file, and practiced basic Git commands by making three meaningful commits.

Submission: Screenshots of the project folder and three-commit history.